  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations to Montana totaled $858M in FY2026 to date. Award activity shows 5,571 awards with an average award size of $154K. Obligations fell 25.1% year over year. Recent fiscal years show a peak and partial retrenchment: FY21 was $691M, FY22 was $925M, FY23 was $1B, FY24 was $1.1B, FY25 was $1.1B, and FY26 is $858M. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $309M, followed by the Department of Agriculture with $198M and the Department of Homeland Security with $149M. Top vendors include S & K SECURITY GROUP LLC at $115M and ARCHER WESTERN FEDERAL JV at $58.8M. Key industries by obligation are Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $120M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $117M. This snapshot reflects partial-year totals and shows where federal dollars and prime contractors are concentrated in Montana for the current fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are federal buying and vendor relationships in Montana?",
        "body": "Federal buying is concentrated among a few agencies: the Department of Defense leads with $309M, the Department of Agriculture has $198M, and the Department of Homeland Security has $149M. Vendor obligations are also concentrated: S & K SECURITY GROUP LLC received $115M, ARCHER WESTERN FEDERAL JV received $58.8M, and PAF ELECTRICAL, INC. received $57M. The top industries include Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $120M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $117M. That mix shows large program buys and construction and aviation-related spending dominate obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What changed compared with prior fiscal years in Montana federal contracting?",
        "body": "Obligations rose from $691M in FY21 to $1.1B in FY24 and FY25, then moved to $858M in FY26 to date. The current-year totals are partial and obligations are down 25.1% year over year. Average award size in FY26 to date is $154K across 5,571 awards. This pattern shows recent high-water marks followed by a year-to-date decline in obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
